From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:59:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The splash: the welcome message shown as text, once, for at
 most a minute

ImGuiSplash::update passed rtx.welcomeMessage to ImGui::TextWrapped as its printf format: "%s%s%s..." read pointers
off the stack on the render thread. Any server's client Lua sets the option through the Remix API, and
rtx.splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds (unbounded, evaluated every frame against the start time, the epoch when the
splash never started) brought the splash and the welcome window back at once.

- The welcome message is drawn with TextWrapped("%s", ...), as patch 0012 already draws the main splash text.
- rtx.splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds is capped at 60 s (the option's maximum, and again where it is read).
- The splash shows once, as the process starts: it starts only in the first two minutes after the first frame,
  never measures from the epoch, and once its time has passed it is done for the process. The clock is now steady.

RtxOptions.md: the option's maximum.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 RtxOptions.md                        |  2 +-
 src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.cpp | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.h   | 15 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/RtxOptions.md b/RtxOptions.md
index 5eda6957b..c5578ba19 100644
--- a/RtxOptions.md
+++ b/RtxOptions.md
@@ -1064,7 +1064,7 @@ This file is auto-generated by RTX Remix. To regenerate it, run Remix with `DXVK
 |rtx.spatiallyHashedRadianceCache.staleFrameNumber|int|64|||Maximum number of frames without new samples before a SHaRC entry is evicted\.<br>Higher values retain coverage longer but can preserve stale data; SHaRC clamps the effective minimum to 8 frames\.|
 |rtx.spatiallyHashedRadianceCache.targetNumUpdateRecords|int|0|||Target number of update records per frame\. A record is a path vertex that an update path adds to the cache\.<br>The update grid is resized to reach it the way NRC sizes its training grid, which keeps the update cost independent of resolution\.<br>Higher values make the cache converge and respond to lighting changes faster at a higher update cost\.<br>0 disables the target, and downscaleFactor sets a fixed update grid instead\.<br>Quality presets set this target\. Use Custom graphics settings to override it manually\.|
 |rtx.spatiallyHashedRadianceCache.voxelSize|float|0.02|||Base world\-space size of SHaRC voxels\.<br>Higher values produce larger voxels with broader coverage but less spatial detail\.|
-|rtx.splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds|int|12|||The amount of time in seconds to display the Remix splash message for\.|
+|rtx.splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds|int|12||60|The amount of time in seconds to display the Remix splash message for\.|
 |rtx.srgbDither.ditherMode|int|2|||Final output dither mode selection\. Dithering allows for reduction of banding artifacts in the final rendered output from quantization using a small amount of monochromatic noise\.<br>Supported enum values are 0 = None \(Disabled\), 1 = Spatial \(Enabled, Spatial dithering only\), 2 = SpatialTemporal \(Enabled, Spatial and temporal dithering\)\.<br>|
 |rtx.stochasticAlphaBlendAverageSearchMatches|bool|False|||Averages the radiance of up to 4 matching neighbors instead of using the first match, which reduces flicker from per\-frame noise\.|
 |rtx.stochasticAlphaBlendDepthDifference|float|0.1|||Max depth difference for a valid neighbor\.|
diff --git a/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.cpp b/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.cpp
index 47347a310..943e12f4f 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.cpp
@@ -39,33 +39,66 @@ namespace dxvk {
            "When set to true this message will be hidden, otherwise it will be displayed on every launch.");
     // Note: 12 chosen as a default here to allow the message to persist long enough to read in case the user focuses on other information on the screen first (e.g.
     // shader compilation messages, text from the application itself in its startup sequence, etc).
-    RTX_OPTION("rtx", std::uint32_t, splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds, 12, "The amount of time in seconds to display the Remix splash message for.");
+    // NV-DXVK start: at most 60 s (GMod: any server's client Lua sets runtime options through the Remix API)
+    RTX_OPTION_ARGS("rtx", std::uint32_t, splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds, 12, "The amount of time in seconds to display the Remix splash message for.",
+      args.maxValue = ImGuiSplash::kMaxDisplaySeconds);
+    // NV-DXVK end
     RTX_OPTION("rtx", std::string, welcomeMessage, "", "Display a message to the user on startup, leave empty if no message is to be displayed.");
   };
 
   void ImGuiSplash::update(ImFont* largeFont) {
     using namespace std::chrono;
 
+    // NV-DXVK start: the splash shows once, as the process starts (GMod: a server's client Lua sets runtime options, so
+    // neither a long display time nor a late start may bring it, or the welcome message, back over a game)
+    if (m_hasFinished) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const auto now = steady_clock::now();
+    if (!m_hasUpdated) {
+      m_hasUpdated = true;
+      m_firstUpdateTime = now;
+    }
+    if (!m_hasStarted && duration_cast<seconds>(now - m_firstUpdateTime).count() > kStartWindowSeconds) {
+      m_hasFinished = true;
+      return;
+    }
+    // NV-DXVK end
+
     // Should we show the splash message?  Don't if hidden, or if UI already active
     if (!m_hasStarted && !SplashSettings::hideSplashMessage() && RtxOptions::showUI() == UIType::None) {
       // No need to start again
       m_hasStarted = true;
 
       // Record the start time
-      m_startTime = system_clock::now();
+      m_startTime = now;
     }
 
-    const auto elapsedDuration = system_clock::now() - m_startTime;
+    // NV-DXVK start: nothing to time before the splash starts
+    if (!m_hasStarted) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const std::uint32_t displaySeconds = std::min(SplashSettings::splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds(), kMaxDisplaySeconds);
+    // NV-DXVK end
+
+    const auto elapsedDuration = now - m_startTime;
     const auto elapsedMilliseconds = duration_cast<milliseconds>(elapsedDuration).count();
     const auto elapsedSeconds = duration_cast<seconds>(elapsedDuration).count();
 
     assert(elapsedSeconds >= 0);
 
-    if (static_cast<std::uint32_t>(elapsedSeconds) <= SplashSettings::splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds()) {
+    // NV-DXVK start: once its time has passed the splash is done for this process
+    if (elapsedSeconds > static_cast<long long>(displaySeconds)) {
+      m_hasFinished = true;
+      return;
+    }
+    // NV-DXVK end
+
+    {
       // Show the user the time remaining
       // Note: Clamped to ensure the count does not go negative for a frame (as ImGui does not respond
       // to a close request from within an open popup on the same frame).
-      const auto clampedSecondsRemaining = std::max(SplashSettings::splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds() - elapsedSeconds, 0ll);
+      const auto clampedSecondsRemaining = std::max(static_cast<long long>(displaySeconds) - elapsedSeconds, 0ll);
 
       ImGui::SetNextWindowPos(ImVec2(0, 0), ImGuiCond_Always, ImVec2(0.0f, 0.0f));
 
@@ -106,7 +139,9 @@ namespace dxvk {
         ImGui::SetNextWindowPos(ImVec2(viewport->Size.x / 2 - 170, viewport->Size.y / 2 - 60), ImGuiCond_Always);
         if (ImGui::Begin("Welcome Message", nullptr, ImGuiWindowFlags_NoSavedSettings | ImGuiWindowFlags_NoFocusOnAppearing | ImGuiWindowFlags_NoNav | ImGuiWindowFlags_NoMove | ImGuiWindowFlags_NoResize)) {
           std::string message = str::format(SplashSettings::welcomeMessage(), " -- Closing in ", clampedSecondsRemaining);
-          ImGui::TextWrapped(message.c_str());
+          // NV-DXVK start: the message is text, never a printf format (GMod: a server could set it through the Remix API)
+          ImGui::TextWrapped("%s", message.c_str());
+          // NV-DXVK end
         }
         ImGui::End();
       }
diff --git a/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.h b/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.h
index 44fd24a1d..d9c031b9e 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.h
+++ b/src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui_splash.h
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "imgui.h"
 
 #include <chrono>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 
 namespace dxvk {
@@ -40,10 +41,22 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     void update(ImFont* largeFont);
 
+    // NV-DXVK start: the splash shows once, as the process starts (GMod)
+    // The longest rtx.splashMessageDisplayTimeSeconds takes effect.
+    static constexpr std::uint32_t kMaxDisplaySeconds = 60;
+    // A splash that has not started this long after the first frame (hidden, or the Remix menu open) never starts.
+    static constexpr long long kStartWindowSeconds = 120;
+    // NV-DXVK end
+
   private:
     bool m_hasStarted = false;
     std::string m_messageLanguage;
     std::string m_message;
-    std::chrono::system_clock::time_point m_startTime;
+    // NV-DXVK start: a steady clock, the first frame, and done for good once shown (GMod)
+    std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_startTime;
+    bool m_hasUpdated = false;
+    bool m_hasFinished = false;
+    std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_firstUpdateTime;
+    // NV-DXVK end
   };
 }
